  "description": "AM KEYWARD — command line for scripts and tools (decisions T18–T23): reads secrets through the software-client API with an app token kept in the Windows Credential Manager or the macOS Keychain. `keyward get` prints one value, `keyward run` starts a program with values as environment variables, `keyward headers` feeds Claude Code's headersHelper, `keyward import` moves a plain-text secrets file into Keyward without the values passing through an AI agent, and `keyward powershell install` adds a PowerShell SecretManagement vault.",
